# Create a New Rstudio Project 

Organizing work into a dedicated project makes life easier. It streamlines the collaboration process by helping users track changes and setting file paths more conveniently

- In Rstudio, open File > New Project > New Directory/ Existing  
- Name the project 
- Set location 
_ Create project 

Now a clean working directory is set in .Rproj format 

# Create a .qmd file and knit 

A .qmd file is an advanced version of a mark down file which helps generate HTML and PDF versions of the working document. It helps to demonstrate code, visualize plotting with simple text, reference and e.t.c

- Click File > New File > Quarto Document
- Name the title and author 
- Save it as example.qmd

## Set YAML 

At the top of the document you will find the YAML section, nested by "---". This helps you format the file in various ways. We want our file to render into an HTML, therefore we will copy and paste the below - 

---
title: "Example"
format: html
---

Note - A hash(#) can be used at the beginning of a sentence/ word to make it a heading. Try: 

- Writing a heading that says Introduction 
- Followed by a line underneath that says *A line added for example* 

## Knit the file using the Render button at top

